# <CARD_KEY> — correction/cancellation review checklist

Use actual interactive Jira taskList items. Check only observed completed work; preserve existing card content and machine readiness/playbook binding. Usually4–8 meaningful checks suffice. Split preparation and runtime views when the user needs to review a dry-run; do not multiply the same rule into duplicate mandatory gates.

## Preparation

- [ ] Exact municipality/system/entity and invoice UUID/number/period/action list verified from live rows.
- [ ] Applicable unpaid/unprinted/payment, billing/fiscal, exclusive QR/reference and configuration rules pass; N/A receipt work explained.
- [ ] Complete five-file SQL suite, full immutable backup and recovery prepared; matching alternatives distinguished.
- [ ] Independent review/digests and preparation checks pass; preparation checks are labeled separately from runtime.

## Current requested runtime stage

- [ ] Exact current dry-run/commit/restore user grant recorded; do not mark from a stage parameter or invent approval.
- [ ] Applicable concurrency/side-effect controls established; future due dates alone are not a cancellation gate.
- [ ] Actual per-table runtime counts, values and exact affected/removed IDs captured; no expected count represented as an observed run.
- [ ] Actual ROLLBACK/COMMIT and same-session plus fresh full-state verification pass; unique report/receipts posted.

Show NOT RUN until an actual approved live mutation occurs. Keep production commit approval open after a dry-run. A later committed restore is a separate action. Remove checks irrelevant to the card's stage; a SQL-preparation child does not require production commit permission to finish its own work.
